  "description": "Document 113 event contract for the events app/modules/release/commands.py actually emits. 5 of the catalogue's 9 declared Document 15 events are implemented: ReleaseEvaluationCompleted, ReleaseEligibilityChanged, ReleaseHoldPlaced, ProductReleased, ProductRejected. ReworkDispositionApproved, ReprocessDispositionApproved, DestructionDispositionApproved and PostReleaseHoldPlaced are declared in 07_EVENT_CATALOGUE.yaml but have no producing code path -- this module's `_decide_terminal_or_hold()` helper only has two callers (hold, reject); the three non-standard disposition types (rework/reprocess/destruction) and a post-release hold are not yet built. Verified directly against source (both the direct event_type=\"...\" call sites and every caller of the shared decision helper), not assumed.",
